#: ../../upstream/docs/user/badges.rst:2
msgid "Status badges"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/badges.rst:4
msgid ""
"Status badges let you show the state of your documentation to your users."
" They will show if the latest build has passed, failed, or is in an "
"unknown state. They are great for embedding in your README, or putting "
"inside your actual doc pages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/badges.rst:9
msgid "You can see a badge in action in the `Read the Docs README`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/badges.rst:12
msgid "Display states"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/badges.rst:14
msgid "Badges have the following states which can be shown to users:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/badges.rst:16
msgid "**Green**: ``passing`` - the last build was successful."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/badges.rst:17
msgid "**Red**: ``failing`` - the last build failed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/badges.rst:18
msgid ""
"**Yellow**: ``unknown`` - we couldn't figure out the status of your last "
"build."
msgstr ""

